      "whatExisted": "Head sharing - MQA and GQA - which reduces the cache by storing fewer heads.",
      "problem": "Head sharing pays for memory with head diversity, and it still stores full-width keys and values for every position.",
      "mechanism": "Store neither. Project the keys and values down to a small shared latent vector per position, cache that, and reconstruct the per-head keys and values on the fly when attending.",
      "whatItFixed": "The cache shrank far more than head sharing allows, while keeping the heads distinct - the paper reports a 93.3% reduction against its own baseline.",
      "newTradeoff": "Reconstruction is extra arithmetic at every step, the latent width is a new capacity bottleneck, and it interacts awkwardly with RoPE - which is why the design carries a separate small set of dimensions just for position.",
      "buys": "A large cache reduction without giving up head diversity.",
      "givesUp": "Simplicity and some compute; and it must be trained in from the start rather than converted from a checkpoint.",
      "whenToChoose": "Large-scale serving where the KV cache is the binding constraint and you control pretraining.",
